==Strategy==
The main threat in this stage are the Dark Otters, with rather high pushing power and high HP. Thankfully, there are only 4 waves of Dark Otters, so that is essentially the win condition in this stage. With that being said, do bring [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] and [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] to stall and potentially chunk the Dark Otters. The stage is also rather tight on cash until you kill something like the Dark Otter or a Dolphina.

The enemies in this stage have a large number of different traits, so a generalist lineup doesn't do too bad here. Units like [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] and [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat]] will help you with the random other threats like the Relic Doges and the Li'l Bun Buns, and [[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard Cat]] is also a decent pick here due to his cheap cost and being able to outrange all the enemies here. [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] can be sent out every other Dark Otter wave to nuke the entire field and get rid of Li'l Bun Buns and Dolphinas potentially in the way. Bahamut can even go on to attack Jones, which can give you some space.

==Trivia==
*Cursing the Curser's name foreshadowed the next update after its release, [[Version 9.5 Update|version 9.5]], which made the Curse ability usable by players through the introduction of the Curseblast Cannon and [[Kasli the Bane (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasli the Bane]].
*Like all [[Unearthed Artifacts]] stages, Cursing the Curser's Japanese name references an idiom. In this case, the name Mīra Torigā Mīra (ミイラトリガーミイラ, "Mummy Trigger Mummy"), is a play on the idiom ''mīra-tori ga mīra ni naru'' (ミイラ取りがミイラになる, "The mummy-taker becomes the mummy"), which refers to when someone experiences the very thing they were trying to do to others, or becomes what they were trying to take; a classic example is a hunter becoming the hunted.

